{"notes":[{"n":1,"lesson":"too hard = unable, not unwilling","file":true,"phrase":"too hard","meaning":"太难而做不到（能力上的限制），与“不值得”相对。","usage":"表示某人或某群体做不到某事时使用。加上 too 语气更肯定，读者更容易接受。常与 not worth it 对比，二者意思不同。","examples":[{"t":"Climbing to StarClan was too hard for the young cats.","n":"对年轻的猫来说，爬到星族那里太难了。"},{"t":"The exam was too hard, so nobody finished it.","n":"考试太难了，所以没人做完。"},{"t":"I tried to fix the bike, but the chain was too hard to reach.","n":"我想修自行车，但链条太难够到了。"}]},{"n":2,"lesson":"night matches a night scene; clear sky","file":false},{"n":3,"lesson":"from + place to say where someone comes from","file":true,"phrase":"from far away","meaning":"来自远方，说明出身或来处。","usage":"用 from 引出地点，直接说明来源，避免 distant 被理解成“冷淡”。常用于描述某人或某物从哪里来。","examples":[{"t":"The kitten came from far away and didn't know the forest.","n":"这只小猫来自远方，不认识这片森林。"},{"t":"A stranger from far away arrived in the village.","n":"一个来自远方的陌生人来到了村子。"},{"t":"Those birds fly here from far away every spring.","n":"那些鸟每年春天都从远方飞到这里。"}]},{"n":4,"lesson":"confused about why, not about the plot","file":false},{"n":5,"lesson":"become + adjective: got, not went","file":true,"phrase":"got miserable","meaning":"变得痛苦、难受（进入某种状态）。","usage":"英语里表示“变得怎样”常用 get/got 加形容词，go 直译过来不自然。口语和叙述中都常用。","examples":[{"t":"Darkpaw got miserable when StarClan stayed silent.","n":"星族一直沉默，Darkpaw 变得很痛苦。"},{"t":"I got miserable after waiting in the rain for an hour.","n":"在雨里等了一个小时后，我变得很难受。"},{"t":"The kids got bored when the movie went on too long.","n":"电影太长，孩子们变得无聊了。"}]},{"n":6,"lesson":"furious about + reason, not for","file":true,"phrase":"furious about it","meaning":"因某事而生气，about 后接引起生气的事情。","usage":"形容词 furious、angry 等后面用 about 引出生气的原因，不用 for。描述情绪时很常见。","examples":[{"t":"Darkpaw was furious about it.","n":"Darkpaw 对此非常愤怒。"},{"t":"My mom got furious about the broken window.","n":"我妈妈因为那扇破窗户而非常生气。"},{"t":"He was angry about the late bus all morning.","n":"他因为公交车晚点，整个上午都很生气。"}]},{"n":7,"lesson":"third-person -s with singular subject","file":false},{"n":8,"lesson":"it makes sense that: natural way to explain reasons","file":true,"phrase":"it makes sense that","meaning":"这样说得通，合乎情理，用来解释原因或推断。","usage":"用来解释一件事为什么发生，或说明某个推断合理。比 it's natural to be unable to 更地道、更简洁，后面接从句。","examples":[{"t":"It makes sense that they couldn't reach StarClan without moonlight.","n":"没有月光，他们联系不上星族，这说得通。"},{"t":"It makes sense that she's tired after such a long trip.","n":"经过这么长的旅程，她累了，这很合理。"},{"t":"It makes sense that the shop closed early on the holiday.","n":"节假日店铺早关门，这说得通。"}]},{"n":9,"lesson":"a cat was: article and verb fix","file":false},{"n":10,"lesson":"try again: short set phrase for retrying","file":true,"phrase":"try again","meaning":"再试一次，重新尝试。","usage":"表示失败或未成功后重新做同一件事，是最常用的说法。不要用 go for another try 这种直译。","examples":[{"t":"After the first failure, Darkpaw did not try again that night.","n":"第一次失败后，Darkpaw 那天晚上没有再试。"},{"t":"If the door is locked, try again in five minutes.","n":"如果门锁着，过五分钟再试一次。"},{"t":"He failed the test, but he decided to try again next week.","n":"他没通过考试，但他决定下周再考一次。"}]}]}
